// REJECTS: Unexpected token 'Fatal'. Valid alternatives: ['Error', 'Warn']
//
// ~enforcementLevel takes a CLOSED set of two keyword values. Error and Warn are lexer
// tokens of DomainLexerGrammar, not identifiers, so the enumeration is enforced by the
// grammar and the error names both legal values.
//
// The divergence this guards: a rewrite that reads the level as an identifier and maps it
// to the protocol enum later accepts 'Fatal' at parse time. Worse, because both Error and
// Warn ARE also listed in Domain's identifier rule (they are usable as property names),
// the identifier arm is a genuinely tempting implementation -- it makes every existing
// fixture pass.
###Pure
Class fixture::neg::FatalLevel
[
   c1
   (
      ~function: $this.code->length() > 2
      ~enforcementLevel: Fatal
   )
]
{
   code: String[1];
}
